1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,820
Food connects places, but a shared
ingredient never tells the whole story.

2
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:07,460
Sifr invites curious food explorers
to follow those connections,

3
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:09,000
and look closely at the differences.

4
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:12,360
We begin with one hundred sourced recipes.

5
00:00:12,840 --> 00:00:16,300
Follow coconut to Malaysia, then open
this recorded version of nasi lemak.

6
00:00:17,040 --> 00:00:20,720
The map shows occurrences in this
sample, not how an entire country eats.

7
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:23,380
Now compare it with Thai
curry noodle soup.

8
00:00:24,455 --> 00:00:26,060
Coconut milk appears in both.

9
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:28,860
The aligned list reveals
shared ingredients,

10
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:30,840
differences, and each source’s quantities.

11
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:34,780
Those amounts remain visible evidence;
they do not drive this model.

12
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:37,180
Topography, particles and barcode

13
00:00:37,180 --> 00:00:39,660
are three views of the same
ingredient-derived sketch.

14
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:44,320
Select coconut milk, and follow it
across both recipes and between views.

15
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:47,100
Now change its model weight in one recipe.

16
00:00:47,780 --> 00:00:50,980
The shape responds. Compare
the original, then reset.

17
00:00:51,820 --> 00:00:54,760
This is a visual what-if,
with equal starting weights.

18
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:57,600
It does not predict how quantities
or cooking change flavour.

19
00:00:58,580 --> 00:01:01,140
The original Sifr instrument
explored two illustrative dishes.

20
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:05,320
Today’s Atlas extends that work to sourced
recipes and ingredient connections.

21
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:09,000
The ambition is a shared language
for specific prepared versions,

22
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:11,340
informed by tasting evidence
and cultural context.

23
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:16,540
For now, this prototype gives us
a way to begin looking together.

24
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:20,260
What travels, what changes,
and what makes a dish yours?
